    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NXxXwmWLKGiLpnX8uKS4HS)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: based on `main` (which has #541); touches only `sp-see-also` (doc, `.el`, test).\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (cloud sessions cannot rename it); this is #542.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Follow-up to #541: `sp-see-also-show` listed nothing for Sia's litnotes.\n- Cause (likely, not confirmed on the real vault): the citekey was read from `#+reference:`, but Sia's litnotes keep it in `:ROAM_REFS:`, so no `[cite:]` was searched.\n- Fix, in `sp-see-also`:\n  - new `sp-see-also--citekeys`: reads the `:ROAM_REFS:` property (Sia's choice); all keys, forms `@key`, `key`, `cite:key`, `[cite:@a;@b]`; URLs and DOIs skipped. `#+reference:` is no longer read.\n  - **Fallback, only for files below `litnotes/`** (`sp-see-also-directory`) with no `ROAM_REFS` key: the `#+title:` is the key when it is a single key word, otherwise the file name is. Temporary, for litnotes whose title is still the key; files outside `litnotes/` get no fallback.\n  - the cite regexp and the ripgrep search take a list of keys; ripgrep follows symlinks (`-L`).\n  - the view ends with a line when the note has no key.\n- Applies to every litnote with a key, whether or not other notes already link it by `id:`.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): 52 of 52 pass; `tools/check-tangle.sh`: only this doc. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n- Not run: the GUI or the real vault.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] In a litnote with the key in `ROAM_REFS`, `M-x sp-see-also-show`: notes with `[cite:@key]` are listed, marked `[cite]`\n- [ ] In a litnote in `litnotes/` with no `ROAM_REFS` and the key as title, the same notes are listed\n- [ ] Same with a file named `key.org` whose title is a real title\n- [ ] A litnote that also has `id:` backlinks shows both kinds in one group\n- [ ] If still empty: `M-: (executable-find \"rg\")` and `M-: sp-see-also-cite-dirs`\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAogkKS5ZXm1xMTJvL\n",
